WHAT: Adds egraph rules to cancel PtrToInt(IntToPtr(x)) and
IntToPtr(PtrToInt(x)) round-trips.

WHY: Fe's type-safe lowering sometimes inserts pointer-integer casts
that are immediately reversed. Eliminating the round-trip saves 2
instructions per occurrence.

GAS IMPACT: None on rosetta contracts. Fe's object reference system
doesn't generate these patterns — it uses typed objrefs throughout.

TEAM NOTES: Another correct optimization for a pattern that doesn't
appear in practice. The lesson from steps 7-10 is clear: adding
optimizer rules for patterns not present in the actual codebase doesn't
help. The remaining gas overhead is structural, not pattern-matching.
